# Who reviews what. Rendered from `skeletor-new --owner`: a user (`@name`) or a
# team (`@org/team`). A bare `@org` is rejected by GitHub ("Unknown owner") and
# requests no review at all; proto.pilot had five such lines. Without `--owner`
# every rule below is commented out, and `{{CLI}} doctor` reports that nobody owns
# anything: uncomment them with a real owner.
{{CODEOWNER_PREFIX}}*                           {{CODEOWNER}}

# The governance layer. A change here changes how every other change is
# reviewed, so it gets read even when the diff looks mechanical.
{{CODEOWNER_PREFIX}}/.claude/                   {{CODEOWNER}}
{{CODEOWNER_PREFIX}}/.github/workflows/         {{CODEOWNER}}
{{CODEOWNER_PREFIX}}/.pre-commit-config.yaml    {{CODEOWNER}}
{{CODEOWNER_PREFIX}}/scripts/docs/              {{CODEOWNER}}
